  "summary": "Seika (生花) is a form of ikebana. Written with the same kanji characters, it is also pronounced and known as Shōka.",
  "description": "Seika (生花) is a form of ikebana. Written with the same kanji characters, it is also pronounced and known as Shōka.",
  "culturalContext": "The painter Sōami and the art patron and shōgun Ashikaga Yoshimasa were supporters of the style as early as the 15th century. It reached its peak of popularity and artistic development in the 18th century and was formalised in the late Edo period.",
